# ⚡ UniversalRAG

### Multimodal Agentic RAG: chat with your PDFs, spreadsheets, charts and images, with every answer traced back to its source

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10%2B-3776AB?logo=python&logoColor=white)
![Gemini](https://img.shields.io/badge/LLM-Google%20Gemini-4285F4?logo=google&logoColor=white)
![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/API-FastAPI-009688?logo=fastapi&logoColor=white)
![Next.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Frontend-Next.js%2014-000000?logo=nextdotjs&logoColor=white)
![Streamlit](https://img.shields.io/badge/UI-Streamlit-FF4B4B?logo=streamlit&logoColor=white)

</div>

---

## 📖 Overview

Most RAG chatbots only read text. **UniversalRAG** accepts **PDFs, Excel/CSV files, and images**, then uses an **agentic router** to send each question to the specialist best suited to answer it: a text, table, chart, image, or data-analysis agent.

Every response comes back with **verifiable evidence snippets and source citations**, so you can check where an answer came from instead of trusting it blindly. It also remembers the conversation, so follow-ups like *"and what about the previous quarter?"* work without re-uploading anything.

> **No API key? No problem.** UniversalRAG ships with an offline simulation engine, so the app and the full test suite run even without a Gemini key.

---

## ✨ Features

| Feature                       | Description                                                                                  |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Multimodal ingestion**      | PDF, CSV, XLSX/XLS, and PNG/JPG/WEBP/BMP uploads with automatic type detection               |
| **Agentic routing**           | Schema-enforced JSON routing picks one or several agents per question                        |
| **Five specialist agents**    | Text, Table, Chart, Image, and Data (EDA) agents                                             |
| **Mixed-question support**    | Compares sources across modalities, e.g. a chart against a paragraph                         |
| **Conversation memory**       | Resolves follow-up references using the chat history                                         |
| **Evidence and citations**    | Every answer includes source snippets and citations in a standard JSON response              |
| **Session-isolated indexing** | In-memory vector index scoped per conversation                                               |
| **Auto EDA and charts**       | Summary stats, outliers, correlations, bar/histogram/pie/heatmap from raw data               |
| **Two interfaces**            | Streamlit app, or a Next.js frontend backed by a FastAPI server                              |
| **Offline fallback**          | Simulation engine works without an API key                                                   |

---

## 🧠 Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Upload: PDF / Table / Image] --> B[M1 Upload Handling]
    B --> C[M2 Content Extraction]
    C --> D[M3 Embedding and Indexing]
    Q[User Question] --> E[M9 Conversation State]
    E --> F[M4 Agentic Router]
    F --> G1[Text Agent]
    F --> G2[Table Agent]
    F --> G3[Chart Agent]
    F --> G4[Image Agent]
    F --> G5[Data Agent]
    D --> G1
    D --> G2
    G1 & G2 & G3 & G4 & G5 --> H[M6 Answer Generation]
    H --> I[M7 Evidence and Source Tracking]
    I --> J[Answer + Citations]
    J --> E
```

### Modules

| Module  | Responsibility                                                               |
| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **M1**  | Upload handling, MIME and extension detection, file registry                 |
| **M2**  | Content extraction: PDF text, DataFrames, preprocessed images                |
| **M3**  | Embeddings and a conversation-scoped in-memory vector index                  |
| **M4**  | Agentic router: category, intent, target agents, reference resolution        |
| **M5**  | Specialized agents (text, table, chart, image, data)                         |
| **M6**  | Answer generation and multi-agent merging                                    |
| **M7**  | Evidence and source tracking into a standardized response                    |
| **M8**  | Chat interface (Streamlit app and Next.js frontend)                          |
| **M9**  | Conversation state and memory                                                |

### Agents

| Agent     | Handles                                                              | Example question                                         |
| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Text**  | Semantic search and synthesis over PDF text                          | *"What is the main objective of this document?"*         |
| **Table** | Structured queries and aggregations on spreadsheets                  | *"Which product has the highest sales and by how much?"* |
| **Chart** | Vision-based reading of uploaded chart images                        | *"Which month recorded the highest revenue?"*            |
| **Image** | OCR, diagrams, and visual inspection                                 | *"What information is shown in this image?"*             |
| **Data**  | EDA, outliers, correlations, auto-generated charts from raw CSV/XLSX | *"Show me the correlations and any outliers."*           |

